      "sentence": "Adding rolling win-stay/lose-switch/violation-rate features to the K-Means feature set changes held-out ARI materially, from a mean of 0.848 (95% CI [0.845, 0.851]) to 0.719 (95% CI [0.709, 0.728]) across the same 5 folds used for the primary ARI estimate -- the recovered cluster structure is sensitive to this feature addition, not stable. This is an expected property of K-Means in general (unsupervised partitions shift when informative features are added or removed) and does not by itself invalidate the rule-based classify_state_v3 (which was never derived from, or claimed to be, the unique K-Means-optimal partition of any particular feature set). It does mean this control check should not be read as demonstrating that Rolling_Accuracy/Rolling_Switch_Rate/deviation are the singularly correct or complete feature set -- only that the manuscript's own validation (recovering the rule-based labels from these 4 observable features) is internally consistent, not that a different feature choice would necessarily recover the same partition.",
